{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb59FFFs2kVjTPvwM4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recommend neither starting nor dropping SOC 2 yet. Spend a week or two analysing the evidence you already have, then decide against a threshold you set in advance. Right now you're weighing a £60k, six-month commitment on four data points from a single month.\n\n**Why not start now:** Three requests and one lost deal could be a real trend or just a cluster. Those prospects are also enterprise, while your core market is mid-sized companies. Before deciding on SOC 2, the CEO should be clear whether moving into enterprise is the strategy.\n\n**Why not drop it:** Recorded loss reasons usually undercount security problems. Deals that stall in procurement or vendor review often get logged as \"no decision,\" \"went with competitor\" or \"timing.\" So the problem may be bigger than it looks.\n\n**What to do (days, not months):**\n1. **Go back through the 140 lost deals.** Look for security reviews, questionnaires, SOC 2/ISO 27001 requests or procurement stalls. Read the notes, not just the reason codes. Ask sales reps about the larger deals.\n2. **Size it in money.** Add up the lost annual contract value (ACV) where security played a part. Then check the open pipeline: how much of it is enterprise, and how much of that will face a security review?\n3. **Set the threshold now.** For example, if security-related losses plus at-risk pipeline exceed about 3× the £60k (plus ongoing audit costs), start SOC 2. If they don't, put it off and review again in a quarter.\n\n**In the meantime (low cost):** Put together a security pack: policies, pen-test results, a standard questionnaire response and a trust page. Ask enterprise prospects whether a SOC 2 Type I or a committed audit date would be enough. UK and EU buyers may prefer ISO 27001."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3185,"cache_read_input_tokens":5036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3185},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c40da49-f450-4f32-987a-5a01b894eeff","uuid":"30a9f4be-e032-43e8-a375-e7df1ae69b9f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:13:54.718Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvb591bxUPAXuUzyaN4s"}
